{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2379 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "91ad078f10e96ef90790445e5c335e78769277fe894dfa389756bcdc71f11b29" :edb/db-before-t 2378 :edb/db-after-t 2379 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535691 50 #inst "2026-10-09T05:15:48.754Z" 13194139535691 true] [17592186198287 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361565 13194139535691 true] [17592186198287 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361572 13194139535691 true] [17592186198287 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361579 13194139535691 true] [17592186198297 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361551 13194139535691 true] [17592186198297 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361558 13194139535691 true] [17592186361551 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361552 13194139535691 true] [17592186361551 1089 "q-160479" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361551 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535691 true] [17592186361551 1100 "Consider the transformation $T:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)).$ The inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}(x,y)\\to (u(x,y),v(x,y))$ is given by\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x-2y \\\\ 3x+4y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the Jacobian determinant of $T.$" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361551 1113 #uuid "27628907-7081-5da8-aede-025e47e822cd" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361551 1145 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, we're only given ${T}^{-1}.$ So, we compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute $\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)},$ the Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\n- Then, we will compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ using the relation\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $u(x,y)=x-2y$ and $v(x,y)=3x+4y.$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y} & =-2 \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & =3 & \\,\\frac{∂v}{∂y} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 4-(-2)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & ={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361553 13194139535691 true] [17592186361552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361554 13194139535691 true] [17592186361552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361555 13194139535691 true] [17592186361552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361556 13194139535691 true] [17592186361552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361557 13194139535691 true] [17592186361552 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535691 true] [17592186361552 1041 "selection" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361552 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361553 13194139535691 true] [17592186361552 1110 #uuid "988d5c34-4255-5491-b86a-5a34f690605d" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361553 1034 "\\frac{1}{10}" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361553 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535691 true] [17592186361553 1111 #uuid "c1595f12-632b-5b3c-95e9-0350447eb180" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361554 1034 "8" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361554 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535691 true] [17592186361554 1111 #uuid "6e430db2-d77c-5590-902d-89a4bb251f57" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361555 1034 "-\\frac{1}{8}" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361555 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535691 true] [17592186361555 1111 #uuid "aee4612a-d4f6-5a4e-be8b-4e86f4970c33" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361556 1034 "\\frac{1}{5}" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361556 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535691 true] [17592186361556 1111 #uuid "5011f1d0-a38e-5a20-a37a-9940fb268deb" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361557 1034 "-\\frac{1}{5}" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361557 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535691 true] [17592186361557 1111 #uuid "04981726-d6ae-5bc0-a391-07b9bb0389bd" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361558 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361559 13194139535691 true] [17592186361558 1089 "q-160599" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361558 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535691 true] [17592186361558 1100 "Consider all non-critical points of the transformation $T:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)).$ The inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}(x,y)\\to (u(x,y),v(x,y))$ is given by\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}xy \\\\ \\frac{x}{y}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the Jacobian determinant of $T$ in terms of $u$ and $v.$" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361558 1113 #uuid "1c44d369-eda2-5ec5-aced-7745349bc2c9" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361558 1145 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, we're only given ${T}^{-1}.$ So, we compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute $\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)},$ the Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\n- Then, we will compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ using the relation\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}.\n$$\n\n \nHere, we have $u(x,y)=xy$ and $v(x,y)=\\frac{x}{y}.$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & =y & \\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y} & =x \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & =\\frac{1}{y} & \\,\\frac{∂v}{∂y} & =-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}y & x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & -\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =y\\cdot (-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}})-x\\cdot \\frac{1}{y} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x}{y} \\\\  & =-2v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & ={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2v}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361560 13194139535691 true] [17592186361559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361561 13194139535691 true] [17592186361559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361562 13194139535691 true] [17592186361559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361563 13194139535691 true] [17592186361559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361564 13194139535691 true] [17592186361559 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535691 true] [17592186361559 1041 "selection" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361559 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361561 13194139535691 true] [17592186361559 1110 #uuid "06d04f34-2f5d-538d-b1d6-1fbc2be21fee" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361560 1034 "-2u" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361560 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535691 true] [17592186361560 1111 #uuid "a1eea580-21d0-5839-ab38-50a5e0c68b33" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361561 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2v}" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361561 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535691 true] [17592186361561 1111 #uuid "2258f1c5-addb-5ea2-891b-842b271dc179" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361562 1034 "2uv" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361562 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535691 true] [17592186361562 1111 #uuid "a1cb38c2-f74c-5f5d-8b13-9093b21fc5a1" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361563 1034 "-\\frac{2}{v}" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361563 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535691 true] [17592186361563 1111 #uuid "f04e95d7-4387-536a-88a6-bf4d4e7d40d4" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361564 1034 "\\frac{1}{2u}" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361564 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535691 true] [17592186361564 1111 #uuid "36de1c89-2352-5430-af1d-404f6bef6827" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361565 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361566 13194139535691 true] [17592186361565 1089 "q-81273" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361565 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535691 true] [17592186361565 1100 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}\\,\\,v \\\\ u+{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361565 1113 #uuid "82fb995e-103e-58b4-a8e9-4c6b2963c1a3" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361565 1145 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTo find the locations of the critical points of $T,$ we need to solve \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)={u}^{2}\\,\\,v$ and $y(u,v)=u+{v}^{2}.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2uv & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & ={u}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2uv & {u}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 2v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2uv\\cdot 2v-{u}^{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4u{v}^{2}-{u}^{2} \\\\  & =u(4{v}^{2}-u).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.$ So, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =0 \\\\ u(4{v}^{2}-u) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equation $u(4{v}^{2}-u)=0$ defines a pair of intersecting curves in the $uv$-plane: the line $u=0$ and the parabola $u=4{v}^{2}.$" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361567 13194139535691 true] [17592186361566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361568 13194139535691 true] [17592186361566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361569 13194139535691 true] [17592186361566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361570 13194139535691 true] [17592186361566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361571 13194139535691 true] [17592186361566 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535691 true] [17592186361566 1041 "selection" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361566 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361571 13194139535691 true] [17592186361566 1110 #uuid "97bab831-bea4-5641-b592-71f6ea176170" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361567 1034 "The critical points lie on the lines $u=v$ and $u=-v.$" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361567 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535691 true] [17592186361567 1111 #uuid "8c7bbc91-672e-5065-90ed-6f4cfcae53f5" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361568 1034 "The critical points lie on the lines $u=0$ and $u=v.$" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361568 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535691 true] [17592186361568 1111 #uuid "608a4a50-2033-5f0b-8182-d3765999d50a" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361569 1034 "The critical points lie on the parabola $u={v}^{2}.$" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361569 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535691 true] [17592186361569 1111 #uuid "dab7dc2d-fdad-52d7-b3d0-f9468f928f98" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361570 1034 "The critical points lie on the lines $u=0$ and $u=-v.$" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361570 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535691 true] [17592186361570 1111 #uuid "fb9701da-8d00-5c98-89f3-25d170c2a3c6" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361571 1034 "The critical points lie on the line $u=0$ and on the parabola $u=4{v}^{2}.$" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361571 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535691 true] [17592186361571 1111 #uuid "8ae39714-3b2d-5a7c-87f9-5c60a0748571" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361572 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361573 13194139535691 true] [17592186361572 1089 "q-81275" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361572 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535691 true] [17592186361572 1100 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}v(u-1)^{2} \\\\ v{u}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361572 1113 #uuid "60ee3a52-fb55-514c-801a-c8567eb808e9" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361572 1145 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the locations of the critical points of $T,$ we need to solve \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)=v(u-1)^{2}$ and $y(u,v)=v{u}^{2}.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2(u-1)v & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =(u-1)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =2uv & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & ={u}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2(u-1)v & (u-1)^{2} \\\\ 2uv & {u}^{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(u-1)v\\cdot {u}^{2}-(u-1)^{2}\\cdot 2uv \\\\  & =2{u}^{2}(u-1)v-2u(u-1)^{2}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.$ So, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =0 \\\\ 2{u}^{2}(u-1)v-2u(u-1)^{2}v & =0 \\\\ 2u(u-1)v(u-(u-1)) & =0 \\\\ 2u(u-1)v & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $2u(u-1)v=0$ defines the lines $u=0,$ $u=1,$ and $v=0$ in the $uv$-plane." 13194139535691 true] [17592186361573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361574 13194139535691 true] [17592186361573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361575 13194139535691 true] [17592186361573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361576 13194139535691 true] [17592186361573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361577 13194139535691 true] [17592186361573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361578 13194139535691 true] [17592186361573 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535691 true] [17592186361573 1041 "selection" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361573 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361577 13194139535691 true] [17592186361573 1110 #uuid "991e63f3-61c1-556c-af37-2b00ab340180" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361574 1034 "The critical points lie on the lines $u=v,$ and $u=-v.$" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361574 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535691 true] [17592186361574 1111 #uuid "a866c64a-da58-5f63-981d-a08bbce18efb" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361575 1034 "The critical points lie on the lines $u=0,$ and $v=u.$" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361575 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535691 true] [17592186361575 1111 #uuid "72a02ab5-eca4-584f-bbe9-fda4485a4113" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361576 1034 "The critical points lie on the lines $u=0,$ and $u=-v.$" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361576 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535691 true] [17592186361576 1111 #uuid "5ddbce31-cd88-52c7-b21f-b5bc7a0f38d2" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361577 1034 "The critical points lie on the lines $u=0,$ $u=1,$ and $v=0.$" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361577 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535691 true] [17592186361577 1111 #uuid "30a71ce7-5288-5f91-bc6c-2a72f461b759" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361578 1034 "The critical points lie on the lines $u=v$ and $v=0.$" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361578 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535691 true] [17592186361578 1111 #uuid "a5a99e16-b9e7-50c1-ad62-76c391ac6ac2" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361579 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361580 13194139535691 true] [17592186361579 1089 "q-81279" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361579 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535691 true] [17592186361579 1100 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of $T,$ where $T$ is defined as \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}+3{v}^{2} \\\\ u-2v\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361579 1113 #uuid "59e9bc67-c967-5c58-a234-d26582651fa3" 13194139535691 true] [17592186361579 1145 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the locations of the critical points of $T,$ we need to solve \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)={u}^{2}+3{v}^{2}$ and $y(u,v)=u-2v.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =6v \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2u & 6v \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2u\\cdot (-2)-6v\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-4u-6v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.$ So, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =0 \\\\ -4u-6v & =0 \\\\ 2u+3v & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $2u+3v=0$ defines a line in the $uv$-plane." 13194139535691 true] [17592186361580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361581 13194139535691 true] [17592